-- title:
--   An exceptional fibre can be separated by one extra character
-- statement:
--   Let $G$ be a finite abelian group. For a character $\chi:G\to\mathbb C$ write $P_\chi(S)=\sum_{x\in S}\chi(x)$, and for a bank $(\chi_i)$ write $\operatorname{Obs}(S)=(Q_S,(P_{\chi_i}(S))_i)$, where $Q_S(z)$ counts ordered pairs from $S$ summing to $z$. The exact decoder of $(R,o)$ consists of all three-element supports $S$ with $\operatorname{Obs}(S)=(R,o)$. Assume $|G[2]|=2^r$ and let $S$ have three elements with $|\mathcal F(S)|=2|G[2]|$. There is a bank of $r+1$ complex characters for which
--
--   $$T\longmapsto(P_{\chi_i}(T))_{i<r+1}\text{ is injective on }\mathcal F(S).$$
--
--   This is a fibre-specific bank, with the square data already fixed.
-- source:
--   Alexandre Couret, Couret — Additive reconstruction: STROBO-4, singleton collisions and RECOH formal proof artifacts, https://zenodo.org/records/23980513; archive COURET_MATHEMATIQUES_20261105.zip, SHA-256 19a3b59aee930df74cab79c27b29e014843bd17179a26fef1261ed6b5a651ab7; file RECOH/lean/RecohFibreUpper.lean, lines 184–198; source file SHA-256 682ad74687cb91c6b5c8d4f92be42d438a63b3a643e0e0c7a5093423d4d3efdc; theorem Couret.STROBO2TORS.recoh_exists_bank_on_exceptional_fibre

